<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Vespro della Beata Vergine (Claudio Monteverdi)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1610</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Magnificat (André Campra)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1713</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Magnificat (Johann Sebastian Bach)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1723</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting, revised 1733</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Magnificat (Antoine-Esprit Blanchard)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1741</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Magnificat (Vivaldi)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting for soloists, choir and orchestra</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Magnificat, ten settings (Marc-Antoine Charpentier)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Magnificat (C.P.E. Bach)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Magnificat (Anton Bruckner)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Magnificat settings in every major key (Charles Villiers Stanford)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">settings for Anglican Evensong</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Collegium Regale and 17 more settings (Herbert Howells)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">settings for Anglican Evensong</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Den Herren will ich loben (Maria Luise Thurmair)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1954</span><span class="sg-chain-h">German hymn paraphrase, sung to Melchior Teschner's melody of 1613</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Tell Out, My Soul (Timothy Dudley-Smith)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1962</span><span class="sg-chain-h">English paraphrase</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Magnificat (Krzysztof Penderecki)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1974</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting for the 1200th anniversary of Salzburg Cathedral</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Canticle of the Turning (Rory Cooney)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1990</span><span class="sg-chain-h">hymn paraphrase to the Irish tune Star of the County Down</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Magnificat (Dieter Schnebel)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1997</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Magnificat (Kim André Arnesen)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2010</span><span class="sg-chain-h">setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">All-night Vigil, section 11 (Clive Strutt)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2011</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Eastern Orthodox setting</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Laudato si' (Peter Reulein, libretto by Helmut Schlegel)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2016</span><span class="sg-chain-h">oratorio including the full Latin text</span></li></ul></section>
